# Line endings
#
# Every line in a text file ends with an invisible marker, and Windows uses a
# different one from macOS and Linux. Two tools here disagreed about which:
# git checks files out with the Windows marker (core.autocrlf=true), while
# Prettier — run by the prebuild hook before every production build — rewrites
# them to the other one.
#
# The result was that `npm run build` left six files reported as modified with
# a completely empty content diff. Harmless in itself, but it tripped the
# deploy skill's uncommitted-changes guard on every release, and a working tree
# that is always dirty for a known-fake reason is how a real change eventually
# gets discarded along with the noise.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what is text and leave binaries alone; eol=lf makes
# it check text out with the same marker Prettier writes, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
